"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of "},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Faces.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before e in the clockwise order at w, so a face lies to the right of each of its half-edges."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated vertex has none: two disjoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"triangles have four faces."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Planarity/documentation/Planarity/PlanarEmbedding/rightFace(from:alongEd